{
 "id": "2026-11-20-a",
 "title": "A drug lord bought 4 hippos. Now there are 200 🦛",
 "description": "In the 1980s Pablo Escobar brought four hippos to the private zoo at his ranch, Hacienda Napoles. After he was killed by police in 1993, nobody caught them. With warm rivers, food all year and no predators, they bred along the Magdalena River: about 200 today, the largest hippo herd outside Africa, and Colombia's environment minister warned it could reach about 1,000 by 2035. They pollute rivers and compete with manatees, and sterilising them has been slow and costly, so in April 2026 Colombia authorised culling up to 80, while Indian billionaire Anant Ambani offered to move 80 to his Vantara reserve in Gujarat.\n\nSources: AP (Fortune, 13 Apr 2026); Global News (14 Apr 2026); NPR/OPB (8 May 2026); AFP (Malay Mail, 6 Aug 2026).",
